Usage: homi status [<args>]

Report whether a server is holding devices. Reads the state the uPCIe runtime keeps, taking no lock and opening no device, so it disturbs neither I/O nor a runtime that is starting. Exits non-zero until a server is up and its devices are ready.
  
Where <args> include:

  [ --shm_id NUM ]              ; For be=spdk, DPDK shared-memory-id; for be=upcie, --cplane-id
  [ --cplane-id NUM ]           ; For be=upcie, the control-plane server to attach to
  [ --help ]                    ; Show usage / help

See 'homi --help' for other commands

homi - Host-Orchestrated Multi-path I/O -- ver: {major: 0, minor: 7, patch: 5}
